{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question","id":995123,"title":"Killing Blow Question.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-29T02:07:34-07:00","id":995123,"title":"Killing Blow Question.","content":"''When performing a killing blow, you deal damage equal<br /> to your full dice pool plus your weapon modifier. You\u2019ve time<br /> enough to line up your attack so it avoids your victim\u2019s armor.''<br /> <br /> This means that the enemy to whom someone is performing the Killing Blow takes fully the damage without Dice Rolling, or just say that you are not subtracting dices from Defense or Armor when performing a Killing Blow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11988-montgomery-crobes","name":"Montgomery Crobes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T02:33:48-07:00","id":995128,"title":"","content":"The first option. She take all the full dicepool in automatic damage. <br /> A normal surprise attack rolls as normal but without subtracting defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T03:52:03-07:00","id":995144,"title":"","content":"Also is legit when you perform a KILLING BLOW to target the head take the -3 penalty and have the Kindred stunned by causing the Head Wrack Tilt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11988-montgomery-crobes","name":"Montgomery Crobes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T04:00:27-07:00","id":995147,"title":"","content":"If you're in a position to perform a killing blow, stunning your opponent is generally not going to be a concern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T04:02:27-07:00","id":995148,"title":"","content":"I think that the killing blow is designed as you performed the best attack in the best place but with the only purpose to KILL not to stun. So I'd say no. <br /> If you perform a killing blow probably you are going to shoot/strike the head but in order to kill. And you don't have to apply penalities. <br /> Penality for the head strike applies on a normal surprise attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T08:39:50-07:00","id":995216,"title":"","content":"To make it clear, for you to perform a Killing Blow, your victim is either tied or unconscious, or otherwise helpless. It isn't just unaware, it is already completely helpless. So Tilts aren't usually going to be an issue, and if they are an issue, I as ST wouldn't complain about a Tilt being just declared without roll or penalty, if it comes from the damage.<br /> <br /> A Killing Blow occurs when there are absolutely nothing stopping you from doing your best to finish your enemy once and for all, and isn't quite feasible during an actual fight, so it isn't a balance issue. It is just a clear rule to say that if nothing can stop you of cutting out the head of the fallen enemy, then you just cut it off without needing to lose time rolling dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T08:48:53-07:00","id":995222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995216#post995216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To make it clear, for you to perform a Killing Blow, your victim is either tied or unconscious, or otherwise helpless. It isn't just unaware, it is already completely helpless. So Tilts aren't usually going to be an issue, and if they are an issue, I as ST wouldn't complain about a Tilt being just declared without roll or penalty, if it comes from the damage.<br /> <br /> A Killing Blow occurs when there are absolutely nothing stopping you from doing your best to finish your enemy once and for all, and isn't quite feasible during an actual fight, so it isn't a balance issue. It is just a clear rule to say that if nothing can stop you of cutting out the head of the fallen enemy, then you just cut it off without needing to lose time rolling dice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was in the middle of posting something like this, but you beat me to it! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T08:53:55-07:00","id":995223,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's kind of funny there actually is a rule for that to be honest. Usually, when you have an unconscious or helpless character and a player declares they finish them off, they just kill them outright. It's plausible that a physically weak character with little to no fighting skills wouldn't be able to kill such a character in one blow, but it's not like it changes much. The only few cases where I could see this rule come up is if someone is trying to stop a human sacrifice or somebody is holding someone hostage and they decide to kill the hostage. Then, you'd have maybe one turn or two (more if the person has no weapon skills) to save them assuming they're dedicated enough they will prioritize killing the victim rather than fend the player off. I guess it's also possible that you'd want to finish off a character that was rendered unconscious in a battle and have to worry about doing it quickly enough that you don't get jumped (but they're likely to already be pretty badly hurt anyway, so the big damage would probably be overkill).<br /> <br /> If it comes up, then, you actually have a rule that is pretty much tailor made for that, and somehow, I guess I have to applaud that. I can say it's never happened in my games, though, frankly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T09:03:31-07:00","id":995227,"title":"","content":"The other thing is that taking a -3 to the blow only reduces the targets effective size by one for the purpose of the stun tilt, which just requires that you equal or exceed their size.<br /> <br /> So if you're going to do enough damage to stun with a killing blow after removing three successes, you don't <i>need</i> to bother with the penalty. You're effectively just shaving off two successes for no benefit whatsoever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T09:06:26-07:00","id":995229,"title":"","content":"It will first sate the thirst of the rules-lawyers who are dedicated enough to demand such a thing (I know of STs that would simply demand that you roll each attack until you finish the enemy, just for the sake of it). Secondly it makes a rule for when it is dramatically relevant to know if the target died in the first blow. It is quite a deadly rule, indeed, but still one with some chance of survival if the killer isn't quite good at it, or if the target is hugely resilient.<br /> <br /> And since there is the trope of the survivor of a murder attempt who lives on through playing dead, I'm not against this rule at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T09:22:52-07:00","id":995236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995229#post995229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And since there is the trope of the survivor of a murder attempt who lives on through playing dead, I'm not against this rule at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus if they're not &quot;automatically dead&quot; it gives, say, Kindred the opportunity to Embrace a Touchstone or somebody they don't want to die and don't think they can take the time to heal them conventionally (&quot;Shit, ain't no ghouling that'll fix a punctured lung...&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T12:21:39-07:00","id":995297,"title":"","content":"I'd let Killing blow possible also if the victim is not bound or unconscious but if she is stopped in her position.<br /> So, in a combat, where the victim is fighting vs someone else or vs you before you go with obfuscate, I'd not allow killing blow (because the target is moving).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T13:19:12-07:00","id":995315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995223#post995223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's kind of funny there actually is a rule for that to be honest. Usually, when you have an unconscious or helpless character and a player declares they finish them off, they just kill them outright. It's plausible that a physically weak character with little to no fighting skills wouldn't be able to kill such a character in one blow, but it's not like it changes much. The only few cases where I could see this rule come up is if someone is trying to stop a human sacrifice or somebody is holding someone hostage and they decide to kill the hostage. Then, you'd have maybe one turn or two (more if the person has no weapon skills) to save them assuming they're dedicated enough they will prioritize killing the victim rather than fend the player off. I guess it's also possible that you'd want to finish off a character that was rendered unconscious in a battle and have to worry about doing it quickly enough that you don't get jumped (but they're likely to already be pretty badly hurt anyway, so the big damage would probably be overkill).<br /> <br /> If it comes up, then, you actually have a rule that is pretty much tailor made for that, and somehow, I guess I have to applaud that. I can say it's never happened in my games, though, frankly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the cases where you actually need rules for killing someone who is powerless to prevent it are so edge, I have never needed them in any RPG. But they do exist in most RPGs anyway. It's one of those things where I could imagine a scenario where it would be relevant, so it's kind of nice to know it's there, but such a scenario hasn't actually happened in my experience.<br /> <br /> That, and as Monte pointed out, it's a GM-proofing feature, cause we've all met that one guy who insists you make every roll even when the outcome is inevitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-29-2016, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T13:22:55-07:00","id":995316,"title":"","content":"There<i> is</i> a werewolf merit that lets you use a killing blow on anyone with 0 defense. It's got a load of prerequisites and you need to be in gauru to use it, but the fluff is &quot;You end the fight. Immediately.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T13:54:25-07:00","id":995327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995316#post995316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There<i> is</i> a werewolf merit that lets you use a killing blow on anyone with 0 defense. It's got a load of prerequisites and you need to be in gauru to use it, but the fluff is &amp;quot;You end the fight. Immediately.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. Scary Merit, that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T15:02:34-07:00","id":995368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995297#post995297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd let Killing blow possible also if the victim is not bound or unconscious but if she is stopped in her position.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems... remarkably lethal in an already fairly offense favoring system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995315#post995315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, and as Monte pointed out, it's a GM-proofing feature, cause we've all met that one guy who insists you make every roll even when the outcome is inevitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I have an idea of where it originated as this: staking a sleeping vampire.<br /> <br /> Staking a vampire with a roll is pretty hard in either edition. And vampires (to GM-proof against auto-death during the day) have rolls to wake up if they're in danger. If you have to roll to stake a sleeping vampire, there's good odds they'll just wake up before you finish. It's kind of hard to have the iconic &quot;group of humans finally get to the vampire's lair during the day and stake the monster,&quot; scene if most of the time the vampire wakes up and deals with the mortals however they prefer to. The Killing Blow rules made it so that staking a vampire in their sleep would be a fairly reliable tactic.<br /> <br /> From there, it seems pretty reasonable to have as a general rule in case it comes up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T15:16:27-07:00","id":995374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995368#post995368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I have an idea of where it originated as this: staking a sleeping vampire.<br /> <br /> Staking a vampire with a roll is pretty hard in either edition. And vampires (to GM-proof against auto-death during the day) have rolls to wake up if they're in danger. If you have to roll to stake a sleeping vampire, there's good odds they'll just wake up before you finish. It's kind of hard to have the iconic &amp;quot;group of humans finally get to the vampire's lair during the day and stake the monster,&amp;quot; scene if most of the time the vampire wakes up and deals with the mortals however they prefer to. The Killing Blow rules made it so that staking a vampire in their sleep would be a fairly reliable tactic.<br /> <br /> From there, it seems pretty reasonable to have as a general rule in case it comes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mhmm, that is indeed a situation where it would be useful that is definitely common enough in CofD to warrant a rule for. Hasn't come up for me because I usually use gameline-neutral antagonists like Horrors and Ephemeral Entities in mortal games, but I can definitely see it as fairly common for other groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T17:59:19-07:00","id":995456,"title":"","content":"This is a game where you can have superhuman durability and regeneration, wouldn't surprise me if there were many creatures that could survive a killing blow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T20:09:05-07:00","id":995485,"title":"","content":"Let's say a human stumbles upon a sleeping vampire. Strength 3, Weaponry 4, one applicable specialty, and weapon mod 2 would deal ten damage.<br /> It's enough to kill most humans who don't receive immediate first aid, but you'd have to search in order to find a vampire with only five health levels. You'd have to find one with Size 4 and a single dot of Stamina in order to lethal in the last health box with a dice pool that's not that bad by human standards.<br /> <br /> I believe that scenario is the most likely for a killing blow when it comes to vampires, and if it's that hard for a somewhat above average human to deal full lethal to the weakest vampire I could come up with... Now if the vampire has some reasonable stats like Size 5, Stamina 3 and Resilience 3, the same human would have to strike three times, hoping the vampire fails to wake up from the obvious attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T21:08:35-07:00","id":995494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995485#post995485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say a human stumbles upon a sleeping vampire. Strength 3, Weaponry 4, one applicable specialty, and weapon mod 2 would deal ten damage.<br /> It's enough to kill most humans who don't receive immediate first aid, but you'd have to search in order to find a vampire with only five health levels. You'd have to find one with Size 4 and a single dot of Stamina in order to lethal in the last health box with a dice pool that's not that bad by human standards.<br /> <br /> I believe that scenario is the most likely for a killing blow when it comes to vampires, and if it's that hard for a somewhat above average human to deal full lethal to the weakest vampire I could come up with... Now if the vampire has some reasonable stats like Size 5, Stamina 3 and Resilience 3, the same human would have to strike three times, hoping the vampire fails to wake up from the obvious attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Killing-blow rules would apply, alright, but the scenario you'd usually encounter here is the mortal hammering a stake thru the Kindred's heart in his Haven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T03:51:17-07:00","id":995575,"title":"","content":"In that case, I'd probably add that hammering a stake takes more than one turn. You have to line up the stake and strike it with the hammer. And that's the only way I'd allow for the full damage because staking a vampire by just jamming the stake in their torso would require a lot of strength. You'v most likely have to break the ribcage unless you had a very thin stake that could slip through them. Plus, a stake is wood, so not the hardest thing ever to pierce flesh and bone. The other way would be to go from under the ribcage, but that's a lot more flesh to pierce so still a hammer sounds pretty essential.<br /> <br /> Plus, if it's about hammering a stake, I'm not sure weaponry is the best skill. Craft sounds like it could make sense, and medicine would definitely be more appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T04:10:18-07:00","id":995576,"title":"","content":"Flesh isn't that tough. Just need a decent hardwood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T04:14:01-07:00","id":995577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995575#post995575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case, I'd probably add that hammering a stake takes more than one turn. You have to line up the stake and strike it with the hammer. And that's the only way I'd allow for the full damage because staking a vampire by just jamming the stake in their torso would require a lot of strength. You'v most likely have to break the ribcage unless you had a very thin stake that could slip through them. Plus, a stake is wood, so not the hardest thing ever to pierce flesh and bone. The other way would be to go from under the ribcage, but that's a lot more flesh to pierce so still a hammer sounds pretty essential.<br /> <br /> Plus, if it's about hammering a stake, I'm not sure weaponry is the best skill. Craft sounds like it could make sense, and medicine would definitely be more appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ribcage resistence is already considered in the five damage required to reach the heart. <br /> The killing blow simply means that the attacker have the time to deal his blow at the best of his ability (strenght+weaponary). <br /> So definetely hammer is not necessary to deal a killing blow but it would give an equipment bonus for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T05:31:41-07:00","id":995589,"title":"","content":"I know it is, but it still seems very optimistic to me. According to those rules and the killing blow rules, someone with strength 3 (a bit above human average) and 2 weapons could pierce a vampire's ribcare and stake them right in the heart in one turn with no particular effort. In a fight I can sorta accept that because people are moving. A well times blow can take advantage of the attacker's strength and the opponent's momentum. In a killing blow scenario, all the attacker has is their own strength. Unless, like I suggested, we're talking about a really really sharp stake in a relatively sturdy wood and thin enough to fit through the ribs, I just find that ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Ok, wait, I forgot the -3 penalty for targetting. If we accept that it substract from the successes, then yes, why not. We might be talking about a human with strength 3 and weaponry 5 or Strength 4 and weaponry 4 (or St 5 and W 3), which is a lot rarer and more impressive. The rule also states the five damage must be done in a single attack, so a less skilled hunter would just not be able to stake the vampire without more tools (or help I guess). That sounds right to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","user":"S. Brechen","date":". 10-30-2016, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T05:58:09-07:00","id":995592,"title":"","content":"Ironically, the splat that can most easily stake a vampire in combat is another vampire. Get Vigor 4 and spend a vitae and if it hits, you're in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T06:04:15-07:00","id":995594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995589#post995589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it is, but it still seems very optimistic to me. According to those rules and the killing blow rules, someone with strength 3 (a bit above human average) and 2 weapons could pierce a vampire's ribcare and stake them right in the heart in one turn with no particular effort. In a fight I can sorta accept that because people are moving. A well times blow can take advantage of the attacker's strength and the opponent's momentum. In a killing blow scenario, all the attacker has is their own strength. Unless, like I suggested, we're talking about a really really sharp stake in a relatively sturdy wood and thin enough to fit through the ribs, I just find that ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Ok, wait, I forgot the -3 penalty for targetting. If we accept that it substract from the successes, then yes, why not.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it's perfectly realistic according to me. Strenght 3 means have the strenght to lift more then 100 kg and ribcage does not full covering the chest, and the heart is not right behind the sternum (the skill to hit between ribs is covered by weaponary).<br /> It seems pretty ok to me that a str. 3 and brawl 2 man could stake an immobile vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 10-30-2016, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T06:08:47-07:00","id":995596,"title":"","content":"An average Dalu-form werewolf is strength 3 (because an average human is strength 2 and the form grants you a +1 bonus) and they're <i>always</i> described as being ripped as fuck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T06:51:54-07:00","id":995608,"title":"","content":"Well, whatever rocks your boat I guess. Humans can go up to 5 strength so for me that's like powerlifter level strength (of course powerlifters would be stiff as hell in a fistfight, but whatever) and 3 and 4 are gradients between that and 2 which is average. Average as in every day person with not particularly physical job like a desk job. In that sense, I tend to consider that any person that has a job that demands they work out a little has a fair chance of having strength 3. It's not that complicated to find the space between the ribs, but I doubt anything thicker than a big pencil would go in without getting jammed. The best bet is probably to try to get the heart from below. The problem, without a hammer, would be to jam the stake precisely enough that it would go through he heart and not slide around it. You do what you want, but while hammering a stake into a vampire chest with a hammer feels doable for any average person, stabbing said stake in a single turn just doesn't feel right.<br /> <br /> And, yeah, werewolves are scary sure. That said having strength 3 in Dalu wouldn't prevent my werewolf from getting kicked around by a relatively skilled thug with a baseball bat. Ok, that's mostly because we're playing 1e. New rules would be a fight of two assholes missing each other all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T07:52:55-07:00","id":995635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995608#post995608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New rules would be a fight of two assholes missing each other all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, a werewolf can just walk off a few lethal wounds, so they can go straight to an all-out if need be without much risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T08:34:33-07:00","id":995651,"title":"","content":"Didn't Armory or Armory Reloaded have a hack for extended action staking?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T08:38:53-07:00","id":995652,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but it made it so you needed to do the vampire's health in damage. Back when stakes did lethal.<br /> <br /> So effectively it meant staking wasn't a thing, as it was just as effective as using a sword.<br /> <br /> I suppose the hack might actually work <i>now...</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-30-2016, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T09:23:25-07:00","id":995671,"title":"","content":"It would certainly fix the whole &quot;if 5 successes on a called shot to the chest with a stake pierces a vampire's heart, can I do the same thing to a human with a knife?&quot; problem, if you consider it a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T09:36:14-07:00","id":995676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995671#post995671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would certainly fix the whole &quot;if 5 successes on a called shot to the chest with a stake pierces a vampire's heart, can I do the same thing to a human with a knife?&quot; problem, if you consider it a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW, the answer to this is &quot;yes&quot;. The rules given in Vampire for specified targets (which seems to be the only one that mentions hearts) don't actually say &quot;stake&quot;. It just says &quot;weapon&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T10:59:04-07:00","id":995708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995676#post995676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By RAW, the answer to this is &amp;quot;yes&amp;quot;. The rules given in Vampire for specified targets (which seems to be the only one that mentions hearts) don't actually say &amp;quot;stake&amp;quot;. It just says &amp;quot;weapon&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know it is. It's just that piercing the opponent's heart doesn't do anything by RAW beyond the normal damage for the attack unless the target is a vampire and the weapon is a stake. For some folks that might be dissonant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T12:23:52-07:00","id":995740,"title":"","content":"Yes, though people tend to overestimate how deadly various injuries are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9715197\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9715197\" target=\"_blank\"> pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9715197\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9715197 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Getting stabbed in the heart has a ~1/3 chance of survival whether you get full medical attention or not, and ~1/2 if you make it to a hospital. Though getting shot in the heart is worse odds of survival (and guns tend to do way more damage... so there's that).<br /> <br /> IIRC Hurt Locker is supposed to introduce a bleeding Tilt rather than the current &quot;bleed out once you reach full lethal&quot; rules, which would be something to put on a mortal hit in the heart and would probably bridge the narrative gap well enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T15:36:41-07:00","id":995831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995676#post995676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By RAW, the answer to this is &quot;yes&quot;. The rules given in Vampire for specified targets (which seems to be the only one that mentions hearts) don't actually say &quot;stake&quot;. It just says &quot;weapon&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> * A stake must target the heart (\u20133 die penalty to attack rolls) and must deal at least 5 damage in one attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T15:52:48-07:00","id":995840,"title":"","content":"I was talking about the general Specified Targets section:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Arm (\u20132): A damaging hit can Arm Wrack the victim if it<br /> deals more damage than the target\u2019s Stamina<br /> \u2022 Leg (\u20132): A damaging hit can Leg Wrack the victim if it deals<br /> more damage than the target\u2019s Stamina<br /> \u2022 Head (\u20133): A damaging attack can Stun the victim if it deals<br /> at least as much damage as the target\u2019s Size<br /> \u2022 <b>Heart (\u20133): If the attacker does at least five points of damage,<br /> the weapon pierces the opponent\u2019s heart.</b><br /> \u2022 Hand (\u20134): On a damaging hit, the victim suffers Arm Wrack<br /> \u2022 Eye (\u20135): On a damaging hit, the victim is Blinded </div> </div> </div>Nothing about stakes specifically there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T16:11:46-07:00","id":995849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995589#post995589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it is, but it still seems very optimistic to me. According to those rules and the killing blow rules, someone with strength 3 (a bit above human average) and 2 weapons could pierce a vampire's ribcare and stake them right in the heart in one turn with no particular effort. In a fight I can sorta accept that because people are moving. A well times blow can take advantage of the attacker's strength and the opponent's momentum. In a killing blow scenario, all the attacker has is their own strength. Unless, like I suggested, we're talking about a really really sharp stake in a relatively sturdy wood and thin enough to fit through the ribs, I just find that ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Ok, wait, I forgot the -3 penalty for targetting. If we accept that it substract from the successes, then yes, why not. We might be talking about a human with strength 3 and weaponry 5 or Strength 4 and weaponry 4 (or St 5 and W 3), which is a lot rarer and more impressive. The rule also states the five damage must be done in a single attack, so a less skilled hunter would just not be able to stake the vampire without more tools (or help I guess). That sounds right to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're forgetting equipment modifiers afforded by a good stake (+1) and a Hammer delivering it (+2).<br /> <br /> Also? Indeed, the vulnerability that vampires encounter whilst in the throes of the daysleep is a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T16:41:59-07:00","id":995865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995840#post995840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was talking about the general Specified Targets section:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nothing about stakes specifically there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot; Kindred all suffer from the \u201cgreat banes\u201d: fire, sunlight, and stakes through the heart &quot; pg 101<br /> <br /> &quot; A Stake to the Heart<br /> When a wooden stake penetrates the Kindred heart, the<br /> vampire immediately enters torpor. Unlike normal torpor,<br /> he awakens immediately upon the stake\u2019s removal, but not<br /> before. To target the heart, make an attack roll with a \u20133 die<br /> penalty after factoring Defense. If the attack causes five points<br /> of damage, it penetrates the heart.&quot; Pg 105<br /> <br /> I could be wrong.. but if it's a metal sword or a bullet... then it would just do the damage. no other effects. Though a stake puts them into torpor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T17:34:20-07:00","id":995878,"title":"","content":"Yeah, nobody was suggesting otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T21:57:34-07:00","id":995957,"title":"","content":"Right. So, as previously established, by RAW any weapon can pierce any human character's heart with a -3 called shot and 5 or more damage in a single hit, but doing so only has a special mechanical effect if the weapon is a wooden stake and the character is a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T11:43:39-07:00","id":996174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995849#post995849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're forgetting equipment modifiers afforded by a good stake (+1) and a Hammer delivering it (+2).<br /> <br /> Also? Indeed, the vulnerability that vampires encounter whilst in the throes of the daysleep is a big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the stake weapon bonus is 0, but I guess really sharp stake made of hard wood could give an equipment bonus of 1. And the hammer, of course, of course, that's what I was saying. If the character has a hammer, then, anybody who's not totally incompetent could stake the vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=995635#post995635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, a werewolf can just walk off a few lethal wounds, so they can go straight to an all-out if need be without much risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's a good point. I'd have an attack pool of 4 then, which might be enough to get me between 1 and 2 dice (if the thug has no athletics). Not sure that's such a great tradeoff, though. Lethal does regenerate quickly, but not that quickly and I don't wanna get punted by a baseball bat, even if the pain won't last too long, plus if I neglected my defense, I'd get my suit all dirty and damaged, screw that. Last time my character got jumped by two dudes with sticks, he just ran to his car and grabbed the shotgun in the trunk to scare them off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T12:06:54-07:00","id":996193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=996174#post996174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's a good point. I'd have an attack pool of 4 then, which might be enough to get me between 1 and 2 dice (if the thug has no athletics).</div> </div> </div> </div>Which you could guarantee he wouldn't by taking Gauru form. Or, if you prefer to stick with Dalu, just spend a point of Willpower. I don't imagine this random thug has olympic level skill in Athletics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=996174#post996174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure that's such a great tradeoff, though. Lethal does regenerate quickly, but not that quickly and I don't wanna get punted by a baseball bat, even if the pain won't last too long, plus if I neglected my defense, I'd get my suit all dirty and damaged, screw that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, if you hit him with your lethal damage dealing claws and your goal is to get out of there without being hit with a baseball bat, the thug will be Beaten Down and probably not terribly keen to fight back.<br /> <br /> This is also all assuming full combat turns instead of Down and Dirty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/995123-killing-blow-question?p=996174#post996174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last time my character got jumped by two dudes with sticks, he just ran to his car and grabbed the shotgun in the trunk to scare them off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also a perfectly viable tactic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-31-2016, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}